From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 23:46:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] node-executor: hot-replace healthy local generations

Keep a healthy local Node generation serving while a candidate starts, passes health checks, and prepares its source and external packages without importing application code. Promote the ready candidate and close old admission atomically, then retain exact cleanup and surge ownership until the old direct child is reaped. Keep unhealthy, shutdown, and cgroup-pressure retirement immediate.

Serialize temporary overlap across default and application-declared pools with one global surge allowance. Queue and coalesce routine rotations, reserve deployment capacity before commit with exact recoverable claims, roll committed cutovers across pools, and support bounded explicit force reclamation without terminating the only serving generation before promotion.

Reserve the complete steady-plus-surge Node RSS budget, carry signed package-readiness authority, expose bounded lifecycle and coordinator telemetry, and document the composed local-resilience, atomic-package, memory, and pinned-pool contracts. Add focused coverage for candidate readiness, promotion and drain ownership, exceptional cleanup retries, deployment recovery, topology removal, pressure handling, and global capacity serialization.
